==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{m|non|hlæja}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{m|gem-pro|*hlahjaną}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈl̥aiːja/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|aiːja|lang=is}}
*: {{homophones|hlægja|lang=is}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-strong|hló|hlógu|hlegið}}

# {{context|intransitive|lang=is}} to [[laugh]]
#: {{usex|Að '''hlæja''' dátt.|To '''laugh''' heartily.|lang=is}}

====Conjugation====
{{is-conj-s6|hl|æ|j=j|mp=-|pp=-}}

====Derived terms====
* [[hlæja hátt]] (to laugh [[loud]])
* [[hlæja að]]
* [[hlæja hugur við]] (to gladden one's heart)
*: ''Þau tíðindi, er þeim '''hló hugur við'''.''
*:: The tidings, that '''gladdened''' their '''hearts.
* [[skellihlæja]]

====Related terms====
* [[hlátur]]

